[B]About[/B]

Unofficial CyanogenMod 10 (Android 4.1.2 Jelly Bean) port for the LG L4 II E440g, codename [B]vee4ss[/B], SoC MediaTek MT6575 — the same platform as the LG L5 II. Both phones now build from a shared common tree, [B]mt6575-common[/B], so they get the same fixes.

It runs on the stock prebuilt kernel. The vendor HALs (audio, camera, lights, RIL) are loaded through small wrappers in the device tree instead of patching CyanogenMod.

[B]Build 3 news:[/B] the zip now flashes the boot image by itself (no more dd), audio and camera work, video recording no longer stops after a few seconds, the radio comes up (IMEI, baseband), Bluetooth uses LG's stock MediaTek app and transfers files, and the home key LED behaves like stock.

[B]Device specs[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Device: LG L4 II / LG-E440g
[*]Codename: vee4ss
[*]SoC: MediaTek MT6575, ARMv7-A Cortex-A9
[*]GPU: PowerVR SGX531
[*]Display: 3.2" 320×480 HVGA mdpi
[*]Android: 4.1.2 Jelly Bean (JZO54K)
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working (tested on Build 3):[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Boot, display, touchscreen, PowerVR SGX531 hardware acceleration
[*]WiFi (MT6620)
[*][B]Bluetooth[/B] with LG's stock MediaTek Bluetooth app (MtkBt), as on the stock ROM: pairing, sending and receiving files (OPP). Bluetooth turns itself back on at boot.
[*]Audio: speaker and microphone
[*]Camera: photos and video recording (MPEG-4 320×240 with AMR-WB audio), correct colors
[*][B]Home key LED like stock[/B]: color pattern while booting, charging pattern with the screen off, green when full
[*]LCD brightness
[*]Proximity sensor
[*]USB MTP
[*]Internal storage and external microSD
[*]Modem boots, IMEI and baseband shown, SIM detected
[*]ADB root (development build)
[/LIST]

[B]Not tested on Build 3[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Calls, SMS and mobile data: my test unit is carrier-locked, so I could not check them. The radio side (modem, IMEI, baseband, SIM) comes up.
[*]WiFi hotspot and USB tethering (need mobile data)
[*]GPS (the stock GPS daemon is included), FM radio, Bluetooth audio (A2DP), wired headset
[/LIST]

[B]Known issues[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Video uses the software codecs[/B]: recording is limited to 320×240, and only H.264 Baseline and MPEG-4 videos play (most phone and internet videos are H.264 Main/High). The L5 II already uses the MediaTek hardware codecs; this phone needs its own stock codec blobs first.
[*][B]Camera can freeze for a few seconds right after boot[/B]: while Android scans the storage after a reboot, saving a photo can stall the camera app ("not responding"). Wait for it; it recovers once the scan ends.
[*][B]Carrier-locked phones[/B] show "SIM network unlock PIN" with a SIM from another carrier. The ROM cannot remove a carrier lock; tap Dismiss to keep using the phone.
[*][B]MediaScanner crash[/B]: folders on the microSD with Latin-1 encoded names (for example "Imágenes" written by an old PC) make MediaScanner abort. Rename or remove them from a PC.
[/LIST]

[B]Important notes[/B]
[LIST]
[*]This ROM is for the [B]LG-E440g (vee4ss) only[/B], the only variant I could test. Do not flash it on other L4 II variants.
[*]You need an unlocked bootloader and TWRP: see my [B]How To Root and Unlock the Bootloader LG L4 II E440g[/B] guide and the [B]TWRP 3.1.1-0.1 for LG L4 II E440g[/B] thread.
[*][B]Back up your NVRAM[/B] (IMEI and calibration) before flashing any MTK ROM.
[*]GApps: use a Jelly Bean (4.1) package.
[/LIST]

[B]Requirements[/B]
[LIST]
[*]LG-E440g (vee4ss)
[*]Unlocked bootloader + TWRP 3.1.1-0.1 for LG L4 II
[*]At least 30% battery
[*]Full Nandroid backup
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Download:[/B][/SIZE]

[URL="PUT_DOWNLOAD_LINK_HERE"]cm-10-20261025-UNOFFICIAL-vee4ss.zip[/URL]

[CODE]MD5: ef56316539cc5e6f5d3f1a7b02a444bb[/CODE]

[B]Install: clean flash (recommended)[/B]
[LIST=1]
[*]Copy the zip to your microSD.
[*]Boot into TWRP and make a full backup.
[*]Wipe: Data, Cache, Dalvik Cache (your internal storage is kept).
[*]Install the zip. It writes /system and the boot image.
[*]Optional: install a Jelly Bean GApps package.
[*]Reboot System. The first boot takes a few minutes.
[/LIST]

[B]Install: update from Build 2[/B]
[LIST=1]
[*]Boot into TWRP and make a backup.
[*]Install the new zip (no separate boot.img any more).
[*]Wipe Cache and Dalvik Cache.
[*]Reboot System.
[*]On the other phone, forget the L4 II and pair it again: Bluetooth pairings made with older builds were not saved.
[/LIST]

[B]Troubleshooting[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Bootloop after flashing[/B]: wipe Cache and Dalvik Cache in TWRP and reboot.
[*][B]Another phone cannot find the L4 II[/B]: in Settings → Bluetooth tap the phone name to make it visible (2 minutes), or start the pairing from the L4 II.
[*][B]A video says "Can't play this video"[/B]: it is probably H.264 Main/High, which the software decoder does not support yet.
[/LIST]

